Onboarding flow (Paper file "inkling", page "screens"): 1 "Drop something in" → 2 "Kept as it came" (ring of colourful floating photos, copy centred, light blur only) → 3 "Half a memory is enough" (user's favourite) → possibly a follow-up search screen (variations E "Ask in colour, too" and F "It reads your pictures, too" replace the weaker "Everything else fades") → 4 "It's all yours".

Mascot rhythm: big, small, small, big. Screens 1 and 4 show the large cropped blob. Screen 2: the mascot playfully peeks out from behind different moving items at different times, showing different emotions. Search screens: only the mascot's eyes sit in the search bar, as part of the searching/finding animation.

**Why:** The user wants onboarding to be brand-focused, fun and clean at once.

**How to apply:** Keep the mascot hidden behind existing elements, never adding a new layout element; no speech, no pointing at UI. See [[onboarding-mockups-no-chrome]].
